    party's use of any Covered Software that You incorporate in or 
    interface with such Specific Commercial Service is not restricted, 
    limited or conditioned by any additional terms (including without 
    limitation, any terms that differ from or conflict with this License).

    The above does not apply to:

    (i) any use by You for Your internal purposes; and

    (ii) any Covered Software that You receive from a Contributor 
         pursuant to an agreement between You and the Contributor that 
         provides You with rights to use, reproduce, modify, display, 
         perform, distribute and otherwise exploit such Covered Software 
         for purposes other than the purposes permitted under this 
         License.

    For purposes of this Section 2.3(c), the term "Specific Commercial 
    Service" means a service that (a) is commercial in nature, (b) is 
    primarily directed at making a profit, (c) derives revenue, benefit 
    or other value (whether directly or indirectly) from the use of the 
    Covered Software by third parties, (d) provides an online, digital or 
    electronic service to third parties, and (e) such third parties' use 
    constitutes the primary use of the Covered Software for the service.

    "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by or is 
    under common control with You. For purposes of this definition, 
    "control" means (i) the power, direct or indirect, to cause the 
    direction or management of such entity, whether by contract or 
    otherwise, or (ii) ownership of fifty percent (50%) or more of the 
    outstanding shares, or (iii) beneficial ownership of such entity.

(d) Larger Works.
    You may create and distribute a Larger Work by combining Covered 
    Software with other code not governed by the terms of this License, 
    provided that You comply with the conditions of Sections 2.4 and 2.5.

(e) Notice and Attribution.
    If You distribute Covered Software, You must include a copy of this 
