the terms of this License to the maximum extent possible; and (b) 
describe the limitations and the code they affect. Such description must 
be included in the LICENSE file described in Section 3.4, if such file 
exists, or must be included in a LICENSE.txt file in the relevant 
directory if such file exists, or, if such file does not exist, must be 
posted on a conspicuous webpage that is readily accessible by users for as 
long as You distribute the Covered Software.

2.5. Required Notices

When You distribute Covered Software, You must include this License with 
the Source Code Form of the Covered Software, and You must retain the 
LICENSE file and all copyright, patent, trademark, and attribution notices 
that are present in the Covered Software.

When You distribute Executable Form, You must include this License, and 
You must supply a copy of the License with each copy of the Executable 
Form. You may satisfy this requirement by providing a URL to the License 
text, in the form of a hyperlink or equivalent, in any user interface 
that You use to interact with users (if any), a prominently displayed 
notice that this Executable Form is licensed under this License, with a 
hyperlink to the License text.

You may satisfy the notice in Executable Form by including the 
following notice in a readable text file included with the Executable 
Form: "Licensed under the Mozilla Public License Version 2.0 
(http://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/)."

3. Responsibilities
------------------

3.1. Distribution of Source Form

All distribution of Covered Software in Source Code Form, including any 
Modifications that You create or to which You contribute, must otherwise 
comply with the requirements of Sections 2.1 through 2.5, and You must 
ensure that all recipients receive a copy of this License. You may 
distribute the Covered Software in Source Code Form under the terms of 
this License or any later version of this License published by the 
Mozilla Foundation, provided that such later version of the License is 
approved by the Mozilla Foundation as stated in the Mozilla Public License 
Version 2.0 or later.

3.2. Distribution of Executable Form

If You distribute Covered Software in Executable Form then:

(a) such Covered Software must also be made available in Source Code Form, 
    as described in Section 3.1, and You must inform recipients of the 
    Executable Form how they can obtain a copy of such Source Code Form 
    via a customary machine-readable means; and

(b) You must ensure that all recipients receive a copy of this License, 
    and that all recipients are informed that they can obtain a copy of 
    the Source Code Form of such Covered Software.

(c) You must ensure that any modifications to Covered Software included 
    in the Executable Form are also made available in Source Code Form.

3.3. Description of Modified Versions

You may distribute Covered Software in Executable Form under Section 
3.2, or a Modified Version in Source or Executable Form under Section 
3.1, only if You:

(a) satisfy the conditions in Section 3.2 for the Executable Form; and

(b) retain in the Source Code Form all copyright, patent, trademark, and 
    attribution notices from the Source Code Form of the Covered Software, 
    as well as a notice describing the modifications You made; and

(c) describe in the Source Code Form the nature of the description and 
    purpose of any Larger Work, if any.

3.4. Intellectual Property Matters

(a) Third Party Claims.
    If Contributor has knowledge that a license to a third party's 
    intellectual property right is required to exercise the rights 
    granted or attempted to be granted under this License, Contributor 
    must include a text file with the Source Code Form of the Covered 
    Software describing such claim and the party making the claim in 
    sufficient detail that a recipient will know whom to contact. If 
    Contributor obtains such knowledge after the Covered Software is 
    received by the recipient, Contributor shall promptly modify the 
    LICENSE file or any other affected file to include such information 
    and fulfill the requirements of this subsection 3.4(a).

(b) Contributor API.
    If a Contribution is subject to Section 3.3 of the Commons Clause 
    then Contributor must include a text file with the Covered Software 
    that includes a description of the claim and the party making the 
    claim in sufficient detail that a recipient will know whom to 
    contact.

4. Inability to Comply Due to Statute or Regulation
---------------------------------------------------

If it is impossible for You to comply with any of the terms of this License 
with respect to some or all of the Covered Software due to statute or 
regulation then You must: (a) comply with the terms of this License to 
the maximum extent possible; and (b) describe the limitations and the code 
they affect. Such description must be placed in a text file in the same 
directory as the Covered Software, or a hyperlink to such description 
otherwise readily accessible by users for as long as You distribute the 
Covered Software.

